    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "After a two-year bureaucratic marathon, the self-serious umpire has finally had enough of the search juggler's antics. Brussels dismissed the company's fix as a joke, and now a punchline-sized fine is being drafted under European competition law. The verdict drops just before summer break, adding yet another trophy to the EU's collection against Alphabet, proving that in this circus, the headliner keeps getting caught dropping its own balls.",
      "source": {
